    "lane: ai_ld | id_craft | learning_tech | strategy - used for lane floors so",
    "      one loud category cannot crowd out the other three.",
    "",
    "Low-frequency feeds (Thalheimer, Dirksen, Donald Clark) are deliberately kept.",
    "They post rarely but carry high signal; the 7-day window simply skips them",
    "on quiet weeks at the cost of one HTTP request.",
    "",
    "Deliberately NOT here: any Substack. Substack returns 403 to GitHub Actions",
    "runner IPs, so drphilippahardman.substack.com and joshbersin.substack.com",
    "fetch fine from a laptop and never from CI. Leaving one in emits the same",
    "warning every week. The web-search top-up can still surface their articles.",
    "",
    "Also removed for CI-blocking: fosway.com (403 from runner IPs, and its newest post was 450 days old anyway). If a feed starts 403ing in the run warnings week after week, it is blocking datacenter IPs: drop it rather than let a permanent warning train you to ignore warnings."
